>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `SLOW_ASTAR_TAC`

``` hol4
classicalLib.SLOW_ASTAR_TAC : thm list -> tactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Solves a goal by less committing A-star classical search.

`SLOW_ASTAR_TAC thms` uses the cost

``` text
normalized goal size + 5 * search level
```

and therefore has the same fixed level weight, 5, as `ASTAR_TAC`. It
safely saturates the whole state, then expands the first goal with the slow
cascade, retaining unsafe-rule alternatives after instantiating
alternatives are found. Children are eager and there is no dynamic
per-goal pruning. `clasetSearch.node_limit` defaults to 100000 expanded
states; a non-positive value disables the limit.

The theorem list locally processes `SIntro`, `Intro`, `SElim`, `Elim`,
`SDest`, `Dest` and `Del`. Every unmarked theorem is inserted as an
assumption before search starts. Content-bearing generic simplifier
wrappers are unwrapped and inserted; inert generic controls are ignored.

The tactic succeeds only after all goals are closed and the proof replays.

### Failure

Fails if frontier exhaustion or the node limit is reached without a
complete proof. Malformed extra rules can also fail during processing.

### Example

``` hol4
Theorem slow_astar_tac_example:
  (p \/ q) ==> (p ==> r) ==> (q ==> r) ==> r
Proof
  classicalLib.SLOW_ASTAR_TAC []
QED
```

